  {
   "id": 335987,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/f285c67c070bb4cc.jpg\" alt=\"An age structure diagram is shown on a graph.  The x axis is labeled percent of population, the y axis is labeled in increments of 4, starting from 0–4 and ending at 80+, designating age groups of the population.  The left side is male and the right side is female.  The population starts at about 4% of males and females age 0–4, tapers in slightly and budges out for ages 30–34 and 34–39, going beyond 4%.  Then, the percentages taper down until 80+, where the male is about 1% and the females remain at 2%, which is a slightly higher number than their population at 75–79.  The Female population after about 40–44 is stays at a slightly higher population percentage than the males.\"> </p><p>(credit: Quia)\n\nThis diagram shows the age structure for a country.\nAnalyze the age structure and use it to predict the economic status of this country. Explain your reasoning.</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 849520,
     "content_html": "This country is likely to be an economically developing country because it has a fairly even distribution of individuals in all age groups."
    },
    {
     "id": 849519,
     "content_html": "This country is likely to be an economically developed country because it has many more very young people and very few old people."
    },
    {
     "id": 849521,
     "content_html": "This country is likely to be an economically developed country because it has a fairly even distribution of individuals in all age groups."
    },
    {
     "id": 849518,
     "content_html": "This country is likely to be an economically undeveloped country because it has many more very young people and very few old people."
    }
   ],
